course: dictionary
lesson: 5111
title: Who asks the questions?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An interviewer is the person who asks the questions in an interview. You will meet interviewers on TV, on the radio, in newspapers and in job interviews. The interviewer leads the conversation, so the other person does most of the answering.
explain: Interviewer comes from interview with the ending -er, which means a person who does something. An interview is a talk where one person asks questions and the other answers, so the interviewer is the one asking. Check the clues: «The interviewer asked her about school.» Who is doing the asking? The interviewer is.
explain: «Answering a different question to dodge the real one is called a red herring; good interviewers ask the question again.» Dodge means avoid, so a good interviewer does not let the speaker escape. They ask again until the real question gets an answer.
fact: An interviewer is the person who asks the questions in an interview.
fact: Interviewers work on TV, on the radio, in newspapers and in job interviews.
fact: A person who asks people questions for a survey or a study is also called an interviewer.
fact: Some interviewers are friendly, and some are tough: «a tough interviewer» asks hard questions.
fact: «Good interviewers ask the question again» when someone dodges the real question.
exercise: What is the name for the person who asks the questions in an interview? | Witness | Umpire | *Interviewer
exercise: A person who knocks on doors to ask people questions for a survey is an | Gardener | Actor | *Interviewer
exercise: «The interviewer asked the mayor about the new park.» Find and copy the word that means the person who asks questions. | asked | park | mayor | *interviewer
test: «Good interviewers ask the question again.» What does a good interviewer do when someone dodges the question? | Answers the question for them | Stops the interview at once | *Asks the question again | Leaves the room
test: A tough interviewer is one who | *Asks hard questions | Plays football | Only says thank you | Hands out prizes
exam: Jayden says only TV has interviewers. What is true? | Only children can be interviewers | Only TV has interviewers | *Interviewers also work on radio, in newspapers, for jobs and for surveys | Interviewers never ask questions
